$ jailops app install nginx web --image freebsd-151
App nginx installed as jail web (running)
  Version:   1.30.6,3
  Addresses: 10.20.0.10
  Ports:     http 80/tcp at 10.20.0.10:80 (meant for the Internet: jailops expose web 80) HTTP, the default site.
  Access:    closed: nothing reaches it until jailops app allow web --from SOURCE
  Data:      /usr/local/www The sites.
  Config:    /usr/local/etc/nginx/nginx.conf (restart nginx) The server configuration.
  Logs:      access /var/log/nginx/access.log One line per request.
             error /var/log/nginx/error.log
  Snapshot:  app-installed (jailops jail rollback web --scope all --snapshot app-installed goes back to it)
  Steps:     11 done
Notes:
  Put the site under /usr/local/www.

$ jailops expose web 80 --host-port 8080
jail/web exposed: 80/tcp
  IPv4  10.20.0.10   forwarded: host 8080->80 (NAT)

$ jailops list
NAME   STATE     OS        IMAGE         GEN   ADDRESSES    EXPOSED         AUTOSTART   USED   AGE
web    running   freebsd   freebsd-151   g1    10.20.0.10   8080→80/tcp 4   -           -      3h

$ jailops firewall show web
Policies of jail/web: none (the host answers ping and DNS only)

Reaches jail/web

SOURCE     FAMILY   PROTO   PORTS   LIMITED TO   REACH               BY
Internet   4        tcp     80      any          forward host:8080   expose

The jail reaches (default out: allow (no policy says deny))
  Internet:       all
  Host:           DNS and ping
  Other jails:    all
  Other projects: none

attach one: jailops firewall policy attach POLICY web

